---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";

const title = "PMI Thresholds and Mortgage Payments";
const description =
  "When PMI applies, how it affects monthly payments, and how to plan for removal. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-03";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/mortgage-payment-pmi-thresholds" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">PMI thresholds</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>PMI thresholds and mortgage payments</h1>
    <p>
      PMI can add hundreds to a monthly payment when the down payment is below certain thresholds. This guide shows when PMI applies
      and how to plan for removal.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/estimating-pmi-cost">Estimating PMI cost</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-down-payment-impact">Down payment impact</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    reviewedBy="Practical Finance Tools Editorial Team"
    reviewerRole="PMI threshold and payment planning review"
    reviewedOn="2026-04-03"
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when PMI is the reason the payment scenario changes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when the payment difference between two down-payment scenarios is mostly explained by PMI rather than by principal and interest alone.</li>
      <li>If you need the base payment build first, move to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If you need to compare the cost of a larger down payment with affordability or payoff tradeoffs, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Mortgage payment inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount, note rate, and term.</li>
      <li>Taxes, insurance, HOA, and PMI assumptions.</li>
      <li>Escrow rules or reserves used by the lender.</li>
      <li>Time horizon if comparing scenarios.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When PMI is required</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Commonly required when down payment is below 20%.</li>
      <li>Rules vary by loan program and lender.</li>
      <li>Mortgage insurance may continue until a specific equity threshold is met.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to model PMI</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use a conservative PMI rate estimate if you do not have a quote.</li>
      <li>Test multiple down payment scenarios to see PMI impact.</li>
      <li>Plan for removal timing based on the loan program rules.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Ignoring PMI in the payment when putting less than 20% down.</li>
      <li>Assuming PMI drops off automatically on all loan types.</li>
      <li>Using the same PMI rate across different credit profiles.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Removal triggers</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>80% to 78% loan-to-value thresholds are common.</li>
      <li>Some programs require a minimum seasoning period.</li>
      <li>Appraisal-based removal can require a fee.</li>
      <li>Document requests to remove PMI in writing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why PMI changes the comparison</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>PMI can make a small-down-payment option look affordable on principal and interest alone but much less attractive once the full monthly payment is modeled.</li>
      <li>The key comparison is not just the starting payment, but how long PMI stays in place and what it takes to remove it.</li>
      <li>That is why this page belongs between down-payment planning, mortgage-payment modeling, and extra-payment strategy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Inputs to gather</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Current loan balance and original purchase price.</li>
      <li>Estimated home value if you plan to request removal.</li>
      <li>PMI rate or monthly premium from the lender.</li>
      <li>Loan program rules for minimum seasoning.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Expected home appreciation and timeline.</li>
      <li>Extra payment plan to reach 80% LTV faster.</li>
      <li>Cost of an appraisal for early removal.</li>
      <li>Whether the loan type allows automatic removal.</li>
      <li>PMI cost vs savings from a larger down payment.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Base case with current PMI rate and balance.</li>
      <li>Extra payment case to reach 80% LTV sooner.</li>
      <li>Appraisal-based removal cost included.</li>
      <li>No-appreciation case for conservative timing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">Mortgage payment math</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/estimating-pmi-cost">Estimating PMI cost</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-down-payment-impact">Down payment impact</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/when-can-i-remove-private-mortgage-insurance-pmi-from-my-loan-en-202/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          When can I remove private mortgage insurance (PMI) from my loan?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/estimating-pmi-cost">Estimate PMI cost</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Check affordability</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-03</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



